# Pointing Recording Developer Handoff

## Status and source of truth

- Canonical repository: the repository containing this file.
- Delivery branch: `feat/integrated-vr-interactions-recording`.
- Unity project: `signvr_unity/`, Unity `6000.5.6f1`.
- Host project: `vr-sign-host/` (FastAPI backend and React operator console).
- Editor simulation, local artifact writing, host catalog selection, upload validation,
  and workstation tests are implemented.
- Quest 3 hardware acceptance is still required. Editor simulation artifacts are
  integration evidence only and must never enter the real dataset.

`E:\SignVR_Unity` was the live integration workspace used while the headset was
occupied. New development must treat this repository's `signvr_unity/` directory
as canonical so Unity and host changes cannot drift into separate commits.

## Runtime ownership

| Component | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `RecordingRuntimeBootstrap` | Installs the recording services only in `VRroom`; it does not replace the scene or XR rig. |
| `RecordingCoordinator` | Owns the recording state machine, countdown, finalization, reset, pause handling, and completion events. |
| `RecordingSentenceSequence` | Owns the editable six-item local sequence and sentence-to-viewpoint mapping. It auto-advances only after a valid completed Take. |
| `RecordingViewpointController` | Selects one of six disabled reference cameras and aligns the tracked XR view to its world pose. |
| `RecordingViewpointSceneStateController` | Applies deterministic, non-animated environment state. `state_02` opens the safe door and every other viewpoint closes it. |
| `VRPlayerRig` / `RecordingModeController` | Lock locomotion, player-root drift, XR-origin recalibration, and recorder collisions while leaving tracked head and hands free. |
| `MetaBodyMotionRecorder` | Writes 30 Hz JSONL pose frames, applies completion quality gates, and atomically writes metadata. |
| `RecordingSpatialMetadataProvider` | Snapshots the selected viewpoint, world frame, XR origin, tracked head, floor, and alignment error for every Take. |
| `RecordingPromptBubble` | Renders one non-interactive, depth-independent rounded prompt bubble at the HMD viewport's upper left and disables the legacy duplicate recorder canvas. |
| `RecordingHandSkeletonVisualizer` | Reuses the main Interaction SDK hand transforms and mirrors Meta `OVRSkeletonRenderer` with one line per parent-child bone; the hand mesh is hidden while tracking remains active. |
| `RecordingQuestInput` / `RecordingDebugInput` | Map Quest and Editor start/stop, reset, previous-sentence, and next-sentence shortcuts to the same sequence/coordinator commands. |
| `QuestDeviceGateway` | Handles host pairing and UDP commands; paired-host sentence and Take identifiers are authoritative. |
| `QuestTakeUploader` | Uploads only completed, real-pose artifacts and preserves the local backlog until a receipt marker is written. |
| `vr-sign-host` | Owns batches, rounds, formal sentence selection, Take reservation, external video, and final disk layout. |

The detailed scene coordinates and user flow are in
`signvr_unity/Docs/PointingRecording.md`. The cross-process integration notes are
in `signvr_unity/Docs/RecordingIntegration.md`.

## State contract

Normal local flow:

```text
Ready -> Countdown -> Recording -> Finalizing -> Completed
  ^          |                         |
  |          +-- short press ----------+
  |             cancel, no artifact
  +-- invalid/interrupted Take: keep current sentence for retake
```

- A completed artifact raises `TakeCompleted`; the local sequence then loads the
  next sentence exactly once. Input handlers must not advance the sequence again.
- Cancelling during countdown returns to `Ready` and creates no pose artifact. The
  host also releases its empty reserved Take directory.
- Too-short, low-valid-pose, paused, passthrough-interrupted, capture-error, or
  I/O-error Takes never advance the sentence.
- When paired, the host owns `session_id`, `sentence_id`, prompt text, and
  `take_id`. The headset mirrors the matching local sequence entry only for HMD
  progress and viewpoint selection.

## Viewpoint and world-frame contract

- `RecordingViewpoints` contains six disabled reference `Camera` components,
  `state_01` through `state_06`. They are editable world poses, not Quest render
  cameras.
- `CenterEyeAnchor` remains the only `MainCamera` and the only Quest render camera.
- Loading a sentence selects its reference viewpoint. Starting a Take reapplies
  that viewpoint and waits for tracked-head alignment before countdown proceeds.
- `state_02` opens `safe/.../Object_5` and its keypad around a generated left-edge
  hinge by `105` degrees. Switching away restores the exact authored closed pose;
  there is no interaction or animation and repeated switches do not accumulate.
- OVR uses `FloorLevel`; `resetTrackerOnLoad` and `AllowRecenter` are disabled.
- During recording, `VRPlayerRig` holds the authored player root and the aligned
  XR-origin local pose. Runtime floor-height recalibration is corrected without
  freezing normal head rotation or hand motion.
- Every metadata file records `world_frame_id=VRroom-world-v1`, viewpoint pose,
  actual XR/head pose, position error, alignment status, floor Y, tracking origin,
  and XR-origin correction count. Changing this frame requires an explicit data
  migration and a new world-frame ID.

Do not enable a reference camera in an Android build. Editor preview may render a
reference camera, but Quest recording must always use the tracked HMD camera.

## Prompt catalog contract

The same six entries currently exist in two authoring surfaces:

1. `RecordingSentenceSequence` on `VRroom/RecordingViewpoints`, editable in the
   Unity Inspector.
2. `vr-sign-host/backend/app/pointing_sentence_catalog.json`, loaded by
   `vr-sign-host/scripts/start-local.ps1` by default.

For every entry, keep these fields identical and in the same order:

```text
sentence_id, zero-based index, Chinese text, viewpoint_id
```

`sentence_id` values are continuous (`sentence_001` ...), and `viewpoint_id` must
be explicit (`state_01` ...). The old 300-sentence catalog remains at
`backend/app/sentence_catalog.json`; select it only by setting
`SIGNVR_SENTENCE_CATALOG` or `sentence_catalog` in `config/station.json`. Never
reuse an existing batch/round after changing catalog length or ordering.

## Controls

| Action | Quest 3 | Editor simulation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Start, cancel countdown, or stop current Take | Right-controller `A` short press | `Space` short press |
| Reset current sentence/Take state | Hold right-controller `A` for 1.2 seconds | Hold `Space` for 1.2 seconds |
| Load next sentence and its viewpoint | Right-controller `B` while idle | `Right Arrow` or `Tools/SignVR/Simulation/Next Sentence` |
| Load previous sentence and its viewpoint | Left-controller `X` while idle | `Left Arrow` or `Tools/SignVR/Simulation/Previous Sentence` |
| Formal host control | Pedal/operator UI over UDP | Same coordinator state machine |

The HMD bubble shows sentence progress and state. It is deliberately
non-interactive so it cannot contaminate hand interaction data.

## Fixed reference props

The nine pointing references `box`, `box (1)`, `box (2)`, `plate`,
`dragon_plate`, `plate (1)`, `dragon_coin`, `golden_coin`, and
`golden_coin (1)` are visual-only recording anchors. The scene setup explicitly
disables all of their colliders and grab behaviours. Existing rigidbodies are
kinematic, gravity-free, collision-free, and frozen on every axis. Do not make
these objects movable without revising the recording protocol because their
authored positions disambiguate the pointing target.

## Artifact and upload contract

Quest/local output:

```text
Application.persistentDataPath/Recordings/{session}/{sentence}/
  {stem}.pose.jsonl
  {stem}.meta.json
  {stem}.meta.json.uploaded
```

- Sampling rate: 30 Hz.
- Minimum normally completed Take: 15 frames.
- Quest valid-pose ratio: at least 0.90.
- Metadata is written to `.tmp` and atomically renamed after the pose stream is
  closed.
- `editor_simulation=true` or `pose_source_simulated=true` makes an artifact
  permanently local-only.
- The uploader requires `capture_status=completed` and valid frame-quality
  fields. The host independently rejects simulated, interrupted, mismatched, or
  malformed metadata.
- Do not change filenames, IDs, or metadata fields without retaining backward
  compatibility and adding host API tests.

Host output remains under its configured data root:

```text
{data_root}/{batch_id}/{round_id}/{sentence_id}/{take_id}/
  {take_id}.pose.jsonl
  {take_id}.meta.json
  {take_id}.camera.webm
```

## Local development

Open `signvr_unity/Assets/Scenes/VRroom.unity`, then use:

```text
Tools/SignVR/Configure VRroom Player and Physics
Tools/SignVR/Configure Pointing Recording
Tools/SignVR/Validate VRroom Player and Physics
Tools/SignVR/Validate Pointing Recording
Tools/SignVR/Simulation/Toggle Recording
Tools/SignVR/Simulation/Previous Sentence
Tools/SignVR/Simulation/Next Sentence
```

The configure command is idempotent and preserves hand-adjusted transforms of
existing reference cameras. It creates missing cameras only. In Play Mode,
`Space` can run the full simulated start/sample/stop/advance workflow without a
Quest.

First-time host setup:

```powershell
cd vr-sign-host/backend
py -3.12 -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements-lock.txt

cd ../frontend
pnpm install
pnpm build
```

Run the workstation from `vr-sign-host/`:

```powershell
.\scripts\start-local.ps1
```

Operator console: `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.

## Required validation before a push

```powershell
cd vr-sign-host/backend
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q

cd ../frontend
pnpm lint
pnpm build

cd ../../
git diff --check
```

Also verify in Unity:

- compilation is idle with zero console errors;
- `Tools/SignVR/Validate Pointing Recording` passes;
- `Tools/SignVR/Validate VRroom Player and Physics` passes and all nine fixed
  reference props have no active collider, dynamic body, or grab behaviour;
- `VRroom` has six reference cameras and exactly one `MainCamera`;
- switching `state_02 -> state_03 -> state_02` produces identical open-door
  transforms, and the open view shows both coins and plates;
- the prompt background and all text remain visible above the open safe door;
- both main hand sources are selected and contain the expected parent-child
  skeleton bones;
- one Editor simulated Take reaches `Completed`, writes pose/meta files, and
  advances by exactly one sentence;
- the simulated artifact stays out of the upload queue.

## Quest 3 acceptance gate

Do not label this feature device-validated until all items pass on the actual
recording APK and workstation network:

- HMD bubble remains in the upper-left viewport without clipping in normal head
  movement.
- Each of six sentences selects the intended physical scene viewpoint.
- Different wearer heights converge to the same authored world eye position;
  metadata alignment error is within tolerance.
- Head rotation and both tracked hands remain live while locomotion and collision
  response remain disabled.
- Short `A` press starts/stops; pressing during countdown cancels without a Take;
  a hold resets without advancing. Idle `B` and `X` move next/previous exactly once.
- Boxes, plates, and coins remain at their authored transforms for the whole Take.
- `state_02` opens the safe around its left edge, with coins and plates visible;
  leaving that state closes it without transform drift.
- The hand mesh is replaced by the per-bone skeleton while real tracking and pose
  recording continue to use the main left/right hand sources.
- A valid Take advances exactly one sentence. A tracking failure, app pause, or
  passthrough interruption stays on the current sentence.
- Real pose/meta uploads and camera video land in the same host Take directory;
  network interruption leaves a recoverable local backlog.
- Restarting Quest and host does not overwrite an existing Take.

## Extension rules

- Add behavior through the existing coordinator events and component boundaries;
  do not add a second recording state machine or a second XR camera rig.
- Keep host-authoritative and standalone-local paths behaviorally equivalent.
- When adding prompts/viewpoints, update Unity, the pointing JSON catalog,
  validation, documentation, and device acceptance together.
- Preserve every existing candidate Take. Retake means allocating a new Take ID,
  never overwriting files.
- Keep `signvr_unity/Docs/ThirdPartyAssets.md` current. The five newly required
  pointing-scene GLBs still need provenance and redistribution review before a
  public release.
- Keep generated data, station config, virtual environments, frontend builds,
  Unity `Library/Temp/Logs`, and APK/build output out of Git.
